      "Cost cuts both ways. Hosted APIs are pay-per-use with no upfront hardware, cheap to start and scaling smoothly, but potentially expensive at high volume. Local models mean upfront hardware investment and operational cost, but predictable spend that can be far cheaper at scale. High, steady volume favors local economics; spiky or low volume favors the API.",
